# Linear tickets — only when explicitly asked

Prakrit only. When the user is **Akhil**, do not file a ticket unless he asks.
See [`docs/agents/AGENTS-prakrit.md`](docs/agents/AGENTS-prakrit.md) /
[`docs/agents/AGENTS-akhil.md`](docs/agents/AGENTS-akhil.md).

**Do not file a ticket for an issue, bug, idea, or QA finding on your own.**
The captain's default artifact is the **Lavish plan** (`lavish-plan-gate.mdc`),
not a Linear issue. Describing work is a request for a plan, not a ticket.

File one **only** on an explicit instruction — "file a ticket", "log this in
Linear", "ticket:", "create an issue". Then follow the protocol below.

## Protocol

1. Read folder routing: `docs/linear-ticket-system.md` (decision tree + projects).
2. Parse: title, bug vs feature, portal, area, urgency.
3. **Create** via `npm run linear:ticket -- --chat "<captain's words>"` (GraphQL API only).
4. Reply with **PRP-###** and the **full Linear URL**.
5. **Next:** the plan — `npm run workflow:plan -- --chat "…" --ticket PRP-###` (see `lavish-plan-gate.mdc`); the id is a label, no second Linear call.

**Do not use Linear MCP** — `LINEAR_API_KEY` in `.env.local` is required.

## Chat triggers (the ONLY ones)

- "Create a ticket: calendar UI needs work"
- "File this bug in Linear — residents tab crashes"
- "Log a feature request for SMS applications"
- "Ticket:" / "Linear:" prefix

Anything else — a described bug, a screenshot, a QA sweep finding, "this is
broken" — gets a **Lavish plan**, not a ticket.

## Routing (auto)

| Captain mentions… | Project | Milestone |
| --- | --- | --- |
| production, resend, cron, env | 01 — Infrastructure & Ops | Production env / email |
| manager portal, /portal/ | 02 — Manager Portal | matching section |
| resident, /resident/ | 03 — Resident Portal | matching section |
| SMS, inbox, email | 06 — Communication Hub | SMS or Email & Inbox |
| lease, application | 07 — Leases & Applications | … |
| payment, stripe, charge | 08 — Payments & Finance | Charges & ledger |
| assistant, AI | 09 — AI Assistant | Manager assistant |
| listing, wizard | 10 — Listings & Properties | Create wizard |
| calendar, tour | 11 — Calendar & Tours | Manager calendar UI |

Always add labels: `portal:*`, `area:*`, and `Bug` | `Feature` | `Improvement`.

Assignee + priority are auto-inferred (`scripts/linear/triage-rules.mjs`).

## Priority (when filing)

| Level | Use when |
| --- | --- |
| **High** | Blocks core workflow (signup, login, pay, apply, wrong charges) |
| **Medium** | Frequent surface; annoying but completable |
| **Low** | Cosmetic UI, copy, rename, dev tooling — **unless unusable** |

Override: `npm run linear:ticket -- … --priority 2` (1=urgent … 4=low).

UI polish → **Low** by default. Only **High** if the user cannot finish the task.

Full matrix: `docs/linear-ticket-system.md` → **Priority & backlog sort**.

After filing a batch, run `npm run linear:triage` to normalize assignee + priority on open issues.

## Title format

`[Area] Short imperative — user-visible outcome`

## Do not

- File a ticket he did not ask for (a described issue is a plan, not a ticket).
- Use Linear MCP or `cursor agent` for tickets.
- Create tickets without project + milestone.
- Put secrets in descriptions.
- Mark **Done** for a **partial** fix (only some acceptance parts).
- Move issues **back to Backlog** after a peer/captain marked them Done for a verified tip.

## Status (agents)

| When | Status |
| --- | --- |
| Actively coding this issue | **In Progress** |
| Fix commit covers whole ticket + green `tsc`/unit on that tip | **Done** (+ comment SHA) |
| Partial work / parked | **Backlog** |

```bash
npm run linear:comment -- --ticket PRP-### --sha <commit> --lane cursor-1
```

Full matrix: `docs/linear-ticket-system.md` → **Status workflow**.

## Auth

`LINEAR_API_KEY` in `.env.local` — https://linear.app/settings/api
